# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets applies these headers to every STATIC response (every
# prerendered page, /studio/, the /_astro/* files). Not to responses the Worker writes
# itself: the SSR routes (/preview/**, /api/draft-mode/*) get none of them.
#
# Content-Security-Policy (2026-10-24): the /* line below says only frame-ancestors
# here. scripts/build-csp.mjs runs after every build and rewrites THAT LINE in
# dist/client/_headers to add object-src 'none', base-uri 'self' and a script-src
# listing 'self', Pagefind's 'wasm-unsafe-eval', the external script origins the
# pages load and a hash of every inline script on every page (one site-wide list,
# because the page router runs the next page's scripts under the first page's
# policy). Keep that line byte-for-byte or the build fails. default-src is NOT
# set, so images, frames, styles, fonts and fetches are not restricted. The
# Studio detaches the policy (/studio/* below, trap 1). Detail:
# docs/agent/deployment.md ("Security headers").
#
# If a full policy (default-src and the rest) is ever added, the notes below hold.
#
# WHEN YOU DO ADD A FULL CSP, the embedded Studio and the live preview need:
#   connect-src   https://api.sanity.io https://*.api.sanity.io
#                 wss://*.api.sanity.io          (the Studio's realtime channel)
#                 https://*.apicdn.sanity.io
#                 https://sanity-cdn.com https://*.sanity-cdn.com
#                                                (the Studio's module/version ping;
#                                                 blocked, it logs "Failed to fetch
#                                                 version for package")
#   font-src      https://design-system-static.sanity.io   (the Studio's own Inter)
#                 https://fonts.gstatic.com                (brand fonts, if used)
#   style-src     https://fonts.googleapis.com             (brand fonts, if used)
#   img-src       https: data:                             (cdn.sanity.io images)
#   media-src     'self' https://cdn.sanity.io              (the Home hero video)
#   worker-src    'self' blob:                             (the Studio uses blob workers)
#
# TWO TRAPS BEFORE ADDING ANY RULE OTHER THAN /* (PORTS.md card 59, measured under
# `npm run preview` 2026-09-29; reid-design-site's _headers is a tested full CSP):
#
#   1. Rules for DIFFERENT patterns merge, and two Content-Security-Policy headers are
#      both enforced (the browser takes the intersection). A public CSP on /* would
#      still bind /studio/*, so that rule must detach it first and then set its own:
#          /studio/*
#            ! Content-Security-Policy
#            Content-Security-Policy: <the Studio's policy, grants above>
#
#   2. Rules for the SAME path do not add up. @astrojs/cloudflare prepends its own
#      /_astro/* rule at build carrying the immutable year-long Cache-Control, unless
#      a /_astro/* rule here already sets Cache-Control. A second /_astro/* rule
#      without it (e.g. only "! Content-Security-Policy") silently loses the adapter's:
#      hashed assets answer "max-age=0, must-revalidate" and the detach does nothing.
#      So a /_astro/* rule written here always carries the cache line itself:
#          /_astro/*
#            ! Content-Security-Policy
#            Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
#
# This file also has a /_astro/* rule (card 121, below), written per trap 2. Under
# `npm run preview` a /_astro/ file answers "public, max-age=31536000, immutable".
#
# frame-ancestors replaces the legacy X-Frame-Options. 'self' is exactly right
# now that the Studio is EMBEDDED at /studio: the Presentation tool iframes
# /preview/* from the same origin. (Before 2026-08-28 this also listed
# *.sanity.studio for a hosted Studio and the iframe-pane plugin; both are
# retired. Re-add those origins only if you deliberately run a hosted Studio.)

# HSTS without includeSubDomains or preload until the church's own domain is known (audit DEV-L4,
# 2026-10-25): on that domain they would force HTTPS on EVERY subdomain for a year, so an old
# webmail or a CNAME that only speaks HTTP would stop loading. The cutover check in
# docs/agent/deployment.md ("Putting a site on its real domain") says when to add them back.
#
# The second Content-Security-Policy line (form-action) is a SEPARATE policy on purpose: the first
# line must stay byte-for-byte as it is for scripts/build-csp.mjs. Two policies are both enforced,
# so this one only adds "forms may post to this site only". A pasted form that posts elsewhere
# (a PayPal donate button, a mailing-list signup) needs its origin added to that line.
# Permissions-Policy turns off device features no page uses; embeds keep everything else.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  Content-Security-Policy: form-action 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), usb=(), magnetometer=(), gyroscope=()

# Font files for pasted code (PORTS.md card 121). A "Custom code" block runs in a
# sandboxed srcdoc iframe with an OPAQUE origin, and a font load is always a CORS
# request, so without this the frame falls back to system fonts. Public, hashed,
# immutable files: allowing any origin to read them gives nothing away. Trap 2
# above: this rule is for /_astro/*, so it carries the immutable cache line itself.
/_astro/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The Studio keeps only frame-ancestors (trap 1 above): its bundles, blob workers and
# Sanity's own scripts are not in the public pages' script-src.
/studio/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'

# The pre-launch example photos and clip (public/shot-examples/, deleted at launch). A year,
# as Lighthouse asks: without a lifetime the looping clip was fetched again on repeat visits.
# The names are not hashed, so a changed example gets a NEW file name, never the old one.
/shot-examples/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000

# Unhashed files whose names never change (audit DEV-M7, 2026-10-25): a day, then served while it
# revalidates. The text fonts and the textures moved into src/assets, so Vite hashes them and they
# get the year-long /_astro/* rule above. What is left here: the Studio's lettering font and the
# font licences, the share cards and the icons. Never "immutable": these names are fixed.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/og/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
